            <p class="book-excerpt">
              This landmark 1843 sermon by Charles Fitch was the thundering proclamation of the <strong>Second Angel's Message of Revelation 14:8</strong> &mdash;
              <em>Come out of her, My people.</em> Rooted in the Second Angel&rsquo;s message of Revelation 14:8
              (<em>Babylon is fallen</em>), Fitch called God&rsquo;s people to separate from all apostate Protestant churches
              that had rejected the first angel&rsquo;s judgment-hour message. But the call was not only to come <em>out</em> &mdash;
              it was to come <em>back in</em> to the pioneer Advent message: the books, tracts, sermons, and prophecy charts
              of the early Adventists who restored the sealing Sabbath, the Fourth Commandment in the perpetual law of God.
            </p>

