          <div class="bio-content">
            <h3>Herald of the Second Angel</h3>
            <p>
              Charles Fitch was one of the most consequential preachers in the early American Advent movement. Trained as a
              Presbyterian minister, he was converted to William Miller&rsquo;s prophetic understanding of Daniel 8:14 and became
              a fearless herald of the judgment hour.
            </p>
            <p>
              His greatest contribution was the 1843 sermon <em>&ldquo;Come Out of Her, My People&rdquo;</em> &mdash; a thundering proclamation
              that the Protestant churches had become Babylon by rejecting the first angel&rsquo;s message of the imminent second coming.
              The call of Revelation 18:4 was not merely future, Fitch argued &mdash; it was <strong>present duty</strong>.
            </p>
            <p>
              Fitch also co-designed the celebrated <strong>1843 Prophecy Chart</strong> with Apollos Hale, fulfilling Habakkuk 2:2&rsquo;s
              command to &ldquo;write the vision, and make it plain upon tables.&rdquo; These massive illustrated charts were carried to
              campmeetings across America and used to preach Daniel 8:14 to hundreds of thousands.
            </p>
            <p>
              He died on October 14, 1844 &mdash; just eight days before the Great Disappointment &mdash; having given his life
              as one of the foremost voices of the Midnight Cry.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

